                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This was my first foray into the Match 3 genre of games. I didn't really think I'd like this type of game, but Season Match was on sale, so I decided to give it a try. So, I got my feet wet with this game. I probably spent more time on it than seasoned Match 3 players, about 13 hours, but I was learning on the fly. This game made it easy for a novice like myself to do that. After a few levels, I understood the objectives of the game, and was well on my way to nailing it. \n\nI turned off the background music and listened to cable news while playing. I managed to get 100% of the achievements and completed the game. I believe there's a few hundred levels in the game, but I could be wrong. For anyone who hasn't tried Match 3 games, I would say this is probably a good game to start with. It's casual and fun, and a nice way to while away a few hours and zone out. I believe there's a least one other game in this series, and I plan to buy it, and if there are more, I'll probably buy all of them. \n\nSo, I guess I am recommending this game.",
